        <mxCell id="8FHhi0EOuua_JHb90U5a-93" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=48;fillColor=#fff7d6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial;font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;UML notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;+ public &amp;nbsp; - private&lt;br&gt;Filled diamond = composition / ownership&lt;br&gt;Dashed arrow = dependency / uses&lt;br&gt;OrderQueue, OrderHeap and HashTable store Order pointers; they do not own Order objects.&lt;br&gt;TradeLog owns its Trade pointers and deletes them in its destructor.&lt;br&gt;Trade stores order IDs, not Order pointers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Implementation note:&lt;/b&gt; OrderManager creates Orders with new, but the pasted code does not show a container/destructor that deletes those Order objects. Add explicit Order ownership to avoid leaks.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
